SPEC = {'setting': 'Warm hand-painted Japanese animation food illustration; honey wood, ivory ceramics and soft cel shading. No hands, text, diagrams or photorealism. Regular oyster mushrooms: broad fan caps, short lateral stems.', 'steps': ['Preparation on a honey wooden board: regular grey oyster mushrooms (Pleurotus ostreatus), with broad thin fan-shaped grey-tan caps, closely spaced cream gills running onto very SHORT lateral stems. One raw cluster to the side and six small flat torn pieces, each one or two caps, centre stage. A modest trimmed tough root base off to one side and a small paring knife resting on the board. Show irregular feathered thin cap edges and unmistakable regular oyster mushroom anatomy. No thick long cylindrical stems, no king oyster mushrooms, no eringi, no mushroom slices.', 'Battering stage: five small flat pieces of ordinary oyster mushrooms with broad grey-tan fan caps and SHORT lateral stems on an ivory plate, lightly dusted in flour. Beside them, one oyster cap partly submerged in thin ivory tempura batter in a small ceramic bowl resting inside a larger bowl of ice. Resting wooden chopsticks bridge the bowl; no hands. The visible uncoated part has grey fan cap and cream decurrent gills, never a long thick white stem. Tiny lumps in cold loose batter. No cooked mushrooms, no king oysters, no eringi slices.', 'Frying stage: a tall deep stainless pot less than half filled with hot golden oil on a modest hob. Three small flat fan-shaped ordinary oyster mushroom pieces in thin pale tempura batter frying separately with modest bubbles. One broad fan-shaped piece lifted on a wire spider just above oil shows delicate irregular crisp edges and a short lateral stem. Spider handle exits frame, no hands. A wire draining rack beside pot. No long thick mushroom stalks, no king oysters, no eringi slices.', 'Finished ordinary oyster mushroom tempura on warm ivory ceramic plate over paper. Six small separate fan-shaped broad mushroom caps, SHORT lateral stems, airy pale-golden thin crisp tempura batter with irregular frilly edges. One piece torn open exposes a thin grey-tan cap and delicate cream gills and juicy thin mushroom interior, NOT a thick white cylindrical stem. Lemon wedge and small bowl of salt; small dipping bowl in background. Food clearly regular oyster mushrooms, not king oysters, no eringi slices.'], 'hero': 'Finished ordinary oyster mushroom tempura on warm ivory ceramic plate over paper. Six small separate fan-shaped broad mushroom caps, SHORT lateral stems, airy pale-golden thin crisp tempura batter with irregular frilly edges. One piece torn open exposes a thin grey-tan cap and delicate cream gills and juicy thin mushroom interior, NOT a thick white cylindrical stem. Lemon wedge and small bowl of salt; small dipping bowl in background. Food clearly regular oyster mushrooms, not king oysters, no eringi slices.', 'mise': []}
